## OGDRAW Configuration settings

To generate the circular genome map for *Dianthus caryophyllus*, I completed the following workflow using OrganellarGenomeDRAW (OGDRAW):

**Accessed OGDRAW:** I navigated to the official OGDRAW web tool portal.  

**Selected Map Mode:** I selected the standard map mode option.  

**Uploaded Input File:** I uploaded the annotated GenBank file (`NC_039650.1.gb`) containing the sequence and feature coordinates.  

**Configured Map Geometry:** I selected Circular as the genome map type.  

**Set Sequence Source:** I designated Plastid as the sequence source.  

**Detected Inverted Repeats:** I enabled the automatic detection option to allow OGDRAW to identify the inverted repeat boundaries (IRa and IRb).  

**Plotted GC Content:** I selected the option to draw the GC content graph on the inner track.  

**Indicated Transcription Direction:** I enabled the option to display the direction of transcription for all gene features.  

**Included Map Legend:** I selected the option to display the full color-coded legend for gene functional classifications.  

**Annotated Introns:** I selected the option to label intron-containing genes with an asterisk (*).  

**Selected Output Format:** I selected PNG as the primary image output format for displaying in my GitHub README, along with downloading a high-resolution SVG copy.  

**Executed Processing:** I submitted the map generation job and waited for OGDRAW to process the annotations.

